{"id":"2937c88628bb358c","group":"58","path":"58/batch18/58-thm-stationary-sets.md","title":"Stationary Sets","display":"thm-stationary-sets — Stationary Sets","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-stationary-sets","aliases":["58-thm-stationary-sets","Stationary Set Theorem","Stationary Sets Properties"],"display":"thm-stationary-sets — Stationary Sets","depends_on":["[[58-df-nonstationary]]","[[../batch19/58-df-stationary.md]]","[[../batch13/58-df-regular-cardinal.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-stationary-sets"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-stationary-sets</span><span>Stationary Set Theorem</span><span>Stationary Sets Properties</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-stationary-sets — Stationary Sets"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"c9ebeb0ba2298425\" href=\"?note=c9ebeb0ba2298425\" title=\"58-df-nonstationary\">58-df-nonstationary</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"b802c3dd76418d95\" href=\"?note=b802c3dd76418d95\" title=\"../batch19/58-df-stationary.md\">../batch19/58-df-stationary.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"0fbfc19800246e77\" href=\"?note=0fbfc19800246e77\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-regular-cardinal.md\">../batch13/58-df-regular-cardinal.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa,S\\in V\">\\(\\kappa,S\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Stationary}\">\\(\\mathrm{Stationary}\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{NonStationary}\">\\(\\mathrm{NonStationary}\\)</span> are the imported typed predicates</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}stationary\\text{-}sets} \\vdash\n\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\omega&lt;\\kappa\\land S\\subseteq\\kappa\n\\to\\bigl(\\mathrm{Stationary}(S,\\kappa)\n\\leftrightarrow\\neg\\mathrm{NonStationary}(S,\\kappa)\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}stationary\\text{-}sets} \\vdash\n\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\omega&lt;\\kappa\\land S\\subseteq\\kappa\n\\to\\bigl(\\mathrm{Stationary}(S,\\kappa)\n\\leftrightarrow\\neg\\mathrm{NonStationary}(S,\\kappa)\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Stationary sets: &quot;large&quot; in sense of club filter.</li>\n<li>Any nonempty union of stationary subsets is stationary; the\n<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span>-completeness statement belongs instead to the club filter and the\nnonstationary ideal.</li>\n<li>Fodor's lemma gives stationary fibers for regressive maps on stationary sets.</li>\n<li>At inaccessible cardinals, stationary reflection provides canonical reflection points.</li>\n<li>Fodor's lemma: fundamental structural property.</li>\n<li>Reflection: stationary sets &quot;reflect down&quot; for inaccessible cardinals.</li>\n<li>Applications: large cardinals, forcing, reflection principles.</li>\n<li>Mahloness says that the regular cardinals below <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span> form a stationary\nsubset, not that every stationary subset of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span> reflects.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-nonstationary","status":"resolved","id":"c9ebeb0ba2298425","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-nonstationary]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch19/58-df-stationary.md","status":"resolved","id":"b802c3dd76418d95","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch19/58-df-stationary.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch13/58-df-regular-cardinal.md","status":"resolved","id":"0fbfc19800246e77","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch13/58-df-regular-cardinal.md]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\kappa,S\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Stationary}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{NonStationary}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}stationary\\text{-}sets} \\vdash\n\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\land\\omega<\\kappa\\land S\\subseteq\\kappa\n\\to\\bigl(\\mathrm{Stationary}(S,\\kappa)\n\\leftrightarrow\\neg\\mathrm{NonStationary}(S,\\kappa)\\bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"\\kappa","display":false},{"tex":"\\kappa","display":false},{"tex":"\\kappa","display":false}],"bytes":1553,"backlinks":[{"id":"39fc3397fdfa6b91","anchor":"ref-4","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4436","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch18/58-thm-stationary-sets.md|58-thm-stationary-sets]]（batch18）"},{"id":"7334957c6d59eacc","anchor":"ref-264","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[58-thm-0-sharp.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-condensation.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-definability.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-generic-extension.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-is-transitive.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-satisfies-GCH.md]]\n[[58-thm-L-satisfies-ZFC.md]]\n[[58-thm-MM.md]]\n[[58-thm-V-equal-L.md]]\n[[58-thm-V-equals-L.md]]\n[[58-thm-absoluteness-calc